{"posts":[{"id":"quasimodo_p20_476","t":"QM is really a great PA confirmation to enter trades at places you would consider an entry. helps a lot with itchy fingers. if you say \"i will mark areas of interest and wait for price to get there and then watch for a QM for entry\" your chances of a wining trade increase a lot. keep an eye for what the engulf engulfs, to get even better odds (say it engulfs a FL for example). in any case its a good way to build your patience. and make your life easier, use alerts.\n\ngreat examples guys\n\nedit: some examples to illustrate the above","a":"Harry","d":"","n":"#476","p":20,"im":["0ea28cf4aa052639846f567b997a52e1cd8d5182"],"m":476},{"id":"quasimodo_p20_477","t":"Hi DT, Thanks for checking out my charts, as you know I am new to this trading method also but studying hard and trying to grasp the concept and learn it to where it is second nature. So with that said let me pick your brain if you will and in the same breath explain the way i see it. Ok using one of the charts above; You consider this to be a failed QM? How? It has a complete QM pattern (H,L,HH and LL) with a return to supply, then a break of the LL. If you are talking about a failure to return (FTR), That is what makes the pattern valid (right?), after a LL. It is a (FTR) to make a HH. To me that is a text book QM.\n\nAnd this would be a failed QM in my eyes\n\nDT let me know how you see it, thanks again buddy this helps me learn when i explain things.","a":"sassofrass","d":"","n":"#477","p":20,"im":["8f1c830a2cb877527d0dc3ce107a758c6ad06dc8","a4866d808b408dbc5666ca41a671c0a2c0e3b6c8"],"m":477},{"id":"quasimodo_p20_478","t":"sassofrass wrote:\n\nAnd this would be a failed QM in my eyes\n\nHi Sass, your above example is a Diamond - very tricky setup... LP","a":"Les_Paul","d":"","n":"#478","p":20,"im":["a4866d808b408dbc5666ca41a671c0a2c0e3b6c8"],"m":478},{"id":"quasimodo_p20_479","t":"Hi LP, Thanks for the pointer, I haven't started studying the diamond yet, but from a glance it looks like it gets a break above the marked QM to enter in the supply level (not marked on the chart) that the QM didn't reach. So is the Diamond considered a failed QM in some situations? love to hear back from you, sass","a":"sassofrass","d":"","n":"#479","p":20,"im":[],"m":479},{"id":"quasimodo_p20_480","t":"Away\n\nHi SS\n\nAs I said in my previous post to you at the top, I should not have wrote 'failed QM' in the example you have shown I do not consider it to be textbook, as price completely ingnored the QM level which I have already marked on the chart, all I see on this chart is a textbook engulf and RT to FTR trade. If I was taking this trade I would have defo been aware of the QM but probably more focused on the above FTR.\n\nThe HH in your example is very high compared with the real chart example in markeedia. So for me this would be a great trade, just I would not have put much emphasis on the QM.\n\nEDIT: Sas, this is only my view, as you can see these are my very first attempts at this P.A concept, so please do take this with a pinch of salt DT","a":"Aaron","d":"","n":"#480","p":20,"im":[],"m":480},{"id":"quasimodo_p20_481","t":"Away\n\nA few more QM examples:\n\nDetails on the charts.\n\n1.\n\n2.\n\n3.\n\nGood hunting all\n\nDT","a":"Aaron","d":"","n":"#481","p":20,"im":["d2a57247a582e0464c0d72afe2a6818877fcd9af","2c00aad4352683840265f82856516a3dbe4c38b4","c51e2a7ae90c7b1254949e35581da02457e582f0","8d0c30ede9d270a8d502262e35b56e9c9a284970","0740a9372149bafa8788079afc9382dda3aaa405","5a82f52b67abc275423a1c6dabe2da2e7a346bb0","b2cb989eb383bfc7bc49b34fea11c2e0ad09d978"],"m":481},{"id":"quasimodo_p20_482","t":"Away\n\nHere are some more QM setups\n\n1.\n\n2.\n\n3.\n\n4.\n\nAny comment on anything that may be wrong would be most appreciated.\n\nDT","a":"Aaron","d":"","n":"#482","p":20,"im":["2e0a206003f07983a60b3a66764705a15401f439","115141f574de35ff5e4e6da331fb69e077225311","1c8204b5cb704c52671c8ce7424f725c6bb3f371","4661f481d5a9c0629a8b2c42da3a