id":"quasimodo_p20_487","t":"Hey DT, Nice charts, you are posting a lot, any way I have a different perspective for you to see, not saying your wrong in any way, just my opinion, sass\n\nKeep up the good work","a":"sassofrass","d":"","n":"#487","p":20,"im":["38a6af64efeabbf44ca4f0bb75aac5822324d6ce","a9a3c88fd4e42cdc5cbd7f59c384e58b746da7bc"],"m":487},{"id":"quasimodo_p20_488","t":"Away\n\nHi Sass,\n\nYes your QM on the first chart was beautiful, I must be honest I am not 100% when it comes to being symmetrical, allI saw was a low, then a high, then a LL then a hugh HH, with no retracement to the QM level. Thank you for looking at my charts buddy, I appreciate it.\n\nSome more examples I have recorded:\n\n1.\n\n2.\n\nCheers all\n\nDT","a":"Aaron","d":"","n":"#488","p":20,"im":["003b6b4ce9ea3a052eb98acc31aa9cd085150cbe","c687be4e58c63e74d604d48bdb716358f3e1b994","9fbde1cec7c556d7140d5ced379210ee979cdb56","77794fd89037ecba32eb22681e5e280331cc0a2b","66a5f37ce8a6fd3decc92e36f104a1f7ec0fdfb3"],"m":488},{"id":"quasimodo_p20_489","t":"Away\n\nSome more QMs:\n\nDetails on the charts.\n\n1.\n\n2.\n\n3.\n\nDT","a":"Aaron","d":"","n":"#489","p":20,"im":["3e04790cf415a82c9e5a94a8488532cbde2405c1","1ddfb354bc2d2340c90214b65ec33bfa0d2a6079","e7365c1e0181b9b31e4b33739dddabb1efada714","6f8d9246d737f56339fdabe9837cf3e1f87d8d20","a5a3b90f0e273de94f85a2a30dc97435360aa9a3","1254a49ef26dd80480ba8290d849a82b7373c95f","fddf7f630fcae76571bc60594d1944fcb21c0b16"],"m":489},{"id":"quasimodo_p20_490","t":"Here are a few more QM's\n\nThe next 3 charts are fractual off the daily QM check it out\n\nzoomed in to the H1\n\nand finally the M15\n\nThis was not as exciting but it gave a good entry\n\nCheers sass","a":"sassofrass","d":"","n":"#490","p":20,"im":["1611bebe0b1d6112600307ae39e85bf96b2a79b1","78f6fe82c67f9d8b5dd1469c42d95c31f6b76330","74fa58c6b14b351ae741a767bc9cbfc7e44591c2","21e805069609c1a4a63843170cc5d74e1afbc142","765320f87efb5e02c500fb728a0bd07a69d1293f","5af0cc1676e494b12b854deff31da1b95db2edda"],"m":490},{"id":"quasimodo_p20_491","t":"Away\n\nHi Sass,\n\nI have asked a few questions on some of your QMs, see what you think\n\nHere are a few more I noticed today:\n\n1.\n\n2.\n\nCheers\n\nDT","a":"Aaron","d":"","n":"#491","p":20,"im":["aec724049e5adac50c84201203a20ec9d0c6b03d","70eac3119efed12937a1975f3826203a6c770c70","525bc23c0486d5cd80f7f23dc5d2449f522820be","725cd3a6eeafb5f0e1e30646f3285e35067eda83","d0d67c820e503f6a5f629a7b5e0d7d0d6af250db","a3d6008346de2fafed7ea58663ab0b80343ed8d8","e87c24ac21e89b37c7c460ab6d3ccf57792220bd","f502ad7c9bccc08b4149335fd7f97d28d1f4aa97"],"m":491},{"id":"quasimodo_p20_492","t":"Great work DT, nothing to say\n\nHow do you manage entry and stop loss at QM left shoulder level and Head Cap?\n\nUsually I perfer Entry at Head level, because stop loss is well defined, many times I miss trade at left shoulder level because not enough RR if stop loss is beyond head level.\n\nSome basic options are: - if head and shoulder levels are not too far entry at shoulder with stop beyond head - if they are a bit far half position at shoulder and half at head, both SL beyond head level - if they are far: entry at shoulder with tight stop loss beyond shoulder level DP, and if price comes to head taking that little stop loss and re-enter at head level.\n\nWhat do you think?","a":"Andyfx","d":"","n":"#492","p":20,"im":[],"m":492},{"id":"quasimodo_p20_493","t":"Away\n\nHi Andy,\n\nI think if I was to enter at the QM level as per the last chart above, I would have probably had the stop below the RBR below just to be safe. Yes I am with you Andy, I would defo prefer entry at the head level, this would make it a classic textbook engulf trade which I love too.\n\nI have seen with a quite a few QMs, price breaks the actual QM level and goes straight to the head which is normally the DP that engulfs an important high/low depending on which way the trade is.\n\nCheers Andy, cool FL work man, keep it up!\n\nDT\n\nEdit: Yes Andy I totally agree with what you said regarding the options, but the perfect entry for me mate would be the left shoulder being in line with the head.","a":"Aaron","d":"","n":"#493","p":20,"im":[],"m":493},{"id":"quasimodo_p20_494","t":"Agree! Left shoulder and Head level zones overlap is best\n\nI posted this on FL homework too, a textbook QM on M5 in reaction to H1 FL","a":"Andyfx","d":"","n":"#494","p":20,"im":["ceaae00f20d8a62ac352f2236a7e5b5a124ea358"],"m":494},{"id":"quasimodo_p20_495","t":"Away\n\nYes Andy, I see it, did you take the trade?\n\n1 more example for my records\n\nDT","a":"Aaron","d":"","n":"#495","p":20,"im":["bebd29fb29d8a940cbf4618d2d10cbcb547b9d71","bb4ed9c4aaaaaf8ad79f32f1a82528cc1dc9a276"],"m":495},{"id":"quasimodo_p20_496","t":"Nope I didn't. Wasn't on that chart while QM was forming, Anyways I'm always afraid of buying so high, even with those juicy setups. Maybe I have to focus more on what price is DOING than what I think it SHOULD do.\n\nAbout your last M30 Eurgbp chart I was wondering at where the price bounced so good at right shoulder. Wouldn't have expect price bouncing there. Maybe LTF can tell something more, seems like a local FL DP.","a":"Andyfx","d":"","n":"#496","p":20,"im":["259841f47e31aac5a8c5b7a523a07b42996f1980"],"m":496},{"id":"quasimodo_p20_497","t":"Away\n\nAndy,\n\nI think I remember Harry saying something like this, sometimes P.A just does not come back, the big boys have all the liquidity they need, so no need to fake the lows. Do not qoute me on that though\n\nI have looked on the 15 and 5 min TFs and there was nothing telling me to long there, the year was 2002 buddy, have a look for yourself and see what you find\n\nDT","a":"Aaron","d":"","n":"#497","p":20,"im":[],"m":497},{"id":"quasimodo_p20_498","t":"Away\n\nHere are a few more interesting examples:\n\nDetails on the charts:\n\n1.\n\n2.\n\n3.\n\n4.\n\nDT","a":"Aaron","d":"","n":"#498","p":20,"im":["b1a94314057f4230a22dc9a46f9e6524da0d6f4d","c93a1148a87dce79b5b6a65a76509d6ab37d894a","7cf9837313ffc9e0036272c22a3be9b41d63e578","b18f2e4df7aec33a37aec1d31ce9748a867b3f66","0679e6556e901d03e4beacd2ef15f4f134a3ffd2","ee37623faf796445d65e0dc947f9292f1c68d2a7","975421e45303f33201808e753cc4bf99a0266efa","5ab4052a16d87d91c92b2c13e58c14dd1a996b6b","58d11844cdf80c3d8bca7543fc3204520449e968","60eff5ddd41015ea5f1dfc067443c355ff166db8","6e0a38ef18a496e5fcf71eb9bdc72a7e4b7a352e","8a4c1bf70720f1e65b4711a89cee4347d6596563","2205f9e85c690c1ae13d1c1fae5beb71ea6733ef"],"m":498},{"id":"quasimodo_p20_499","t":"Hey DT, some answers for your questions, thanks sass\n\nnow zoomed in","a":"sassofrass","d":"","n":"#499","p":20,"im":["cc62509f1d2b3701bc079e7235bdf765e6debc48","551d3c76c930796a785f0c246b91d1d49f350b5a","64bc51314ff388544dd73773b267005c1bc6bba2"],"m":499},{"id":"quasimodo_p20_500","t":"Away\n\nHi Sass,\n\nGood points and well noted buddy, I was aware of other setups but was purely focusing on your charts as they only had QM setups on.\n\nOn the second chart the engulf you point out would not have been a trade signal for me as the engulf IMO was not significant enough I would have been watching the high above that which was engulfed and then took the DP that engulfed.\n\nCheers\n\nDT\n\n151617181920212223","a":"Aaron","d":"","n":"#500","p":20,"im":["2c4313e15c0737b3a48fcaf2be99f4f4da0da618"],"m":500}],"images":[{"k":"8f1c830a2cb877527d0dc3ce107a758c6ad06dc8","t":"assets/thumbs/8f1c830a2cb877527d0dc3ce107a758c6ad06dc8.webp","f":"assets/images/8f1c830a2cb877527d0dc3ce107a758c6ad06dc8.jpeg","w":1029,"h":861,"b":125127,"o":"8f1c830a2cb877527d0dc3ce107a758c6ad06dc8.jpeg","p":20,"pid":"quasimodo_p20_477"},{"k":"a4866d808b408dbc5666ca41a671c0a2c0e3b6c8","t":"assets/thumbs/a4866d808b408dbc5666ca41a671c0a2c0e3b6c8.webp","f":"assets/images/a4866d808b408dbc5666ca41a671c0a2c0e3b6c8.jpeg","w":777,"h":548,"b":44851,"o":"a4866d808b408dbc5666ca41a671c0a2c0e3b6c8.jpeg","p":20,"pid":"quasimodo_p20_478"},{"k":"d2a57247a582e0464c0d72afe2a6818877fcd9af","t":"assets/thumbs/d2a5